      "id": 1,
      "text": "Middleton was named after settler George Middleton, who established a homestead there in 1885.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/middleton-michigan/",
      "category": "people",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town got its own train station in 1886 on the Toledo, Saginaw & Muskegon Railroad, later part of Grand Trunk.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://99wfmk.com/middleton-michigan/",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Rowley House Museum, a Middleton landmark, sits on the National Register of Historic Places.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.middletonhistory.org/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "The Middleton Area Historical Society, founded in 1974, preserves local history and operates the Rowley House Museum.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.middletonhistory.org/history",
      "category": "culture",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The Rowley House was purchased in 1989 by long‑time resident Gilsie Techam, fulfilling the society’s dream of a dedicated museum space.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.middletonhistory.org/history",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The society hosts annual events like Stroll and Tell Walks and a Pie and Ice Cream Social that doubles as the biggest fundraiser.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
